Z||000000||DXR_DAD||06-27-2000||08:35 PM||||Hey Stimpy, in DaRkLoRD's post about the cards you said your club gets dealerships/shops to sponsor club events?<BR>and give discounts? Can you give GGF a few tips on how to go about this.<P>THANKS <BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||12
Z||000001||stimpy||06-27-2000||10:09 PM||||Whew, got me worried with that topic there! Tought ya might be caught in quicksand or something!<P>As far as the relationships we have with local dealerships, I really don't know who set it up (before my time) but Fergusen Pontiac in Norman OK has hosted our car shows since the first. They also give 20% discount on parts when we name drop FCO. When one of our members mentioned that to All-American Pontiac across town, they state they would match the deal and they have been true to their word.  <P>I would say the best thing is to go to the parts manager (new-car sales won't be as interested) and give them the pitch. The very worst thing they can say is "hell no". At which point you take your opportunity to his competition.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||06-27-2000||10:23 PM||||Well no quicksand but we stuck out here in SSF with no phones, The new Bart Project damaged some of pac bell's underground lines<BR>the whole city was out yesterday. <BR>Ok back to the topic, this type of info my also be of use to those starting new clubs,<BR>so thanks. Are there any other things that your club does? or anything they offer the members?<P>I guess I should have started a new post:<BR>(New Fiero Clubs) or something like that?<P><BR>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||7
